      "content": "I'm stuck on this question: A cricket ball of mass 150 g is thrown horizontally and struck by a bat so it moves in the opposite direction. The average net force is horizontal. The experiment varies contact time, keeping force and initial velocity constant. The graph shows final momentum vs contact time, with a straight line from (0, -?) to (0.01, 0) to (0.03, 4.5). Calculate the magnitude of the initial velocity of the ball. I don't know where to start."
